# ─── Keys & Temps ────────────────────────────────────────
# Private keys belong in ./secrets/ (ignored above), not loose in the tree.
# These patterns stay as a backstop for a key that lands somewhere else by
# accident — but a backstop is not a place to keep one: an ignored file is
# still on disk, still readable by anything running as this user, and still
# picked up by backups and editor plugins.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
# NOT a blanket *.txt. That rule silently excluded two kinds of file that
# belong in the repository:
#
#   ai_core/requirements.lock.txt        the hash-pinned dependency lock
#   eval/golden/*/bug_description.txt    the eval harness's ground truth
#   eval/golden/*/expected_root_commit.txt
#
# The golden dataset was half-committed as a result — the sibling
# expected_fix.patch files were tracked but their .txt counterparts were not,
# so a fresh clone could not run the eval harness at all. An ignore rule that
# matches by extension will keep doing this every time someone adds a file that
# happens to end in .txt; these are the actual scratch outputs.
eval_output.txt
lf_help.txt
stats.txt
*.pid
*.log
*.log*
*.gz
